artifact: s41_mhrx_pullup_off.15f3ae07dae1.{pof,svf}
purpose: STEP 0 PLUS ONE PIN. The LOGIC CPLD's weak pull-up taken OFF pin 74
  (MHRX / G2691 / `M MCU_P17`), so the net falls when the Pi halts and the
  power MCU gets its shutdown acknowledge instead of running to the 60 s
  failsafe. Nothing else is in it.

SHIPPING: yes — no non-shipping switch is set.

built_from: a9e8e05dab48b910216d54f78e39e0dc8a2c9ce0
  branch s41-mhrx-pullup-off = s37-step0-shipping-base (61e38ce3) + ONE qsf
  change. THIS BRANCH MUST NEVER BE MERGED TO main, for its parent's reason:
  it is the shipping design that is on the part, plus the minimum change,
  deliberately WITHOUT main's later logic elements.

the_change: three lines in quartus/dsp4_logic.qsf —
    set_location_assignment PIN_74 -to mhrx
    set_instance_assignment -name RESERVE_PIN "AS INPUT TRI-STATED" -to mhrx
    set_instance_assignment -name WEAK_PULL_UP_RESISTOR OFF -to mhrx
  The global RESERVE_ALL_UNUSED_PINS is UNCHANGED ("As input tri-stated with
  weak pull-up" in both fit reports) and still covers every other unassigned
  pin — the MH/panel UART nets keep the pull-up they need. Pin 74 is the one
  exception, and it is an exception because the CM4 drives that net
  push-pull and the power MCU reads it.

config: (none) — this build.sh (a4ee3d1f's) predates CFG_LINE entirely, the
  same as its parent. Every non-shipping switch is off.

device: 5M1270ZT144C4
logic_elements: 156 / 1,270 (12 %) — IDENTICAL to step 0
pins: 69 / 114 (61 %) — step 0's 68 plus the reserved pin 74
fmax: 70.05 MHz (step 0: 66.1 MHz)
sim_gate: PASS (5 testbenches, the same RTL as step 0 byte for byte)
slot_map: sha256:efd8d555440094b627345b5a84894f9e7a6b569056f4eccb417d42d6ce32182e

md5_pof: 72a28864d54334215d192070d5742252
md5_svf: fc6ce23ed14cda464f277a56cf21ab92

fit_diff_vs_step0: the "All Package Pins" table is 150 lines in both builds
  and differs on EXACTLY ONE ROW:
    - ; 74 ; 112 ; 3 ; RESERVED_INPUT_WITH_WEAK_PULLUP ; ... ; ; no ; On  ;
    + ; 74 ; 112 ; 3 ; mhrx                            ; input ; 3.3-V LVTTL ; ... ; Y ; no ; Off ;
  Every other pin's location, direction, I/O standard, bus hold and weak
  pull-up are byte-identical. Logic element count is identical (156, 28
  registers).

  AND THE FITTER RE-PLACED THE DESIGN, WHICH THE DIFF SAYS OUT LOUD: adding a
  pin constraint re-seeds placement, so LABs go 24 -> 26, peak interconnect
  7.6 % -> 10.6 %, every control signal moves cell (e.g. u_clkgen|Equal1~0
  LC_X10_Y7_N3 -> LC_X6_Y6_N3), and Fmax moves with them. The NETLIST is
  unchanged — same RTL, same 156 LEs, same sim gate — but the placement is
  not, and "only pin 74 changed" is true of the pin table and of the
  function, not of the bitstream bytes. Recorded so that nothing is later
  attributed to a change this artifact does not contain.

reproducibility: built TWICE from clean `git archive` trees. The two pof files
  are BYTE-IDENTICAL (72a28864d54334215d192070d5742252). The svf bodies are
  identical with comment lines removed; quartus_cpf stamps the wall clock into
  the `!Device #1:` comment, as it does for every artifact here (S37-1). The
  pof is the artifact to hash.

  The step-0 baseline was rebuilt in the same session from 61e38ce3 and
  reproduced its recorded pof md5 79284dad6e9c27995f91806056c9fba5 exactly,
  so the fit-report diff above is between two builds of this toolchain and
  not against a report from another machine.

design_id: NONE — for its parent's reason. The design-ID/knock readback block
  costs +124 LEs (S36 §1.1) and would take this artifact from 156 to ~280,
  which is not what a one-pin change is allowed to carry. This bitstream
  identifies itself by the md5 above plus /home/app/logic-flash.log, exactly
  as step 0 and as step 0's own rollback do.

rollback: s37_shipping_step0.c62c024714f2.svf
  md5 d47b74c6c881b82a110491266a6bd31d (svf) / 79284dad6e9c27995f91806056c9fba5 (pof)
  THIS, not dsp4_logic.a1f6672af6c3.svf, is what the bench lives on: S38
  flashed step 0 onto the part on 2026-09-12 and it has been there since.

S41_COMMAND_LINE:
  cd tools/pi
  ./logic_flash.sh --dry-run s41_mhrx_pullup_off.15f3ae07dae1.svf
  ./logic_flash.sh           s41_mhrx_pullup_off.15f3ae07dae1.svf
  # the rollback now defaults to s37_shipping_step0.c62c024714f2.svf.
  # AN_EN (GPIO26) must read low; it does with the gated app (S38-1). No
  # waiver, and GPIO26 is never written.

S41_PROOF:
  * the net, measured through the CM4's own GPIO14 with the PL011 released:
      `pinctrl set 14 ip pn` -> lo   (step 0 read hi)
      `pinctrl set 14 ip pd` -> lo   (step 0 read hi against a ~50 k pull-down)
    then `pinctrl set 14 a0 pn` to put TXD0 back.
  * `sudo poweroff` with the rocker ON: MHRX falls and the power MCU's 5 Hz
    shutdown sequence completes in seconds, not 60 s, then the unit reboots.
  * step 0's own behaviour intact: the converter/option-slot clock pair still
    driven — U3 pin 142 = 12.288 MHz, pin 141 = 48 kHz (J18 P37/P38).
